  "source_notes": [
    "The default stock optics. Its halation block is the 35mm_strong_ah_modelled profile: P0 measured the first version's single-radius additive kernel at a 0.66-0.72 mm half-energy radius against its own declared 0.55 mm, a red-dominant halo even from a blue source, and +0.95% frame-wide red energy.",
    "Grain constants are unchanged from the first version and are still known bad: 60 um blobs, Selwyn slope -0.44, 48 um RMS granularity 87 against ~4 for a real 400-speed stock. P4 replaces the model.",
    "dc_mode is residual: the characteristic curve already contains the uniform-field reflection, so only the spatial part is reinjected.",
    "2026-08-10 F1 fix: gate reference corrected to unity (layer exposure is already grey-normalized), so gate_ev now genuinely means scene EV above box-speed 18% grey. All gates shifted +2.2 EV to preserve the tuned look at film exposure 0; film exposure now moves the trigger in the physical direction."
  ]
